; The shape most domains are actually in.
;
; There is an SPF record, and it only discourages. There is a DMARC record,
; and it only watches. Reports are going somewhere, which is the part that
; matters, but nothing has moved past monitoring in a long time — and there
; is no CAA record at all.
;
; Expected: a middling grade. Everything here is published; almost none of it
; asks a receiver to do anything.

typical.example.        3600 IN MX  10 inbound1.mailhost.example.
typical.example.        3600 IN MX  20 inbound2.mailhost.example.

typical.example.        3600 IN TXT "v=spf1 include:_spf.mailhost.example include:bulk.sender.example ~all"

_dmarc.typical.example. 3600 IN TXT "v=DMARC1; p=none; aspf=r; adkim=r; rua=mailto:dmarc@typical.example"

mh1._domainkey.typical.example. 3600 IN TXT "v=DKIM1; k=rsa; "

typical.example.        3600 IN TXT "google-site-verification=3qW1nQ8pLk7xZr2vUa0bYh4Mc6Jd9FeGsT5uNi1oKpQ"
